efore Rāma). And Rāma saw that one of flaming energy at the head of the ascetics, and the hero said to Lakşınana, enhancer of auspiciousness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.7,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3011019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a7aea30500edbdb6a7d5d014e71d0b4f4c79528f6c831f2bb1ece1fba31d32bd","compact":"60e566733443853fd4056cc51fdd8e31d17c7a624850d69cd3759cf925f025d6","nasal":"60e566733443853fd4056cc51fdd8e31d17c7a624850d69cd3759cf925f025d6"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-11-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":11,"verse":20,"english":"O Laksmana, the revered saint, Agastya, is coming out. I recognize that mass of asceticism by a certain kind of majesty (that characterises him).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.968,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3011020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"26694527b94bb3cad6257e236c94f4ee7fcd634fb8cfc46866f81f14802ddb3f","compact":"22d8e344e26028980834a4d79e039c52d14bd7e356b93b62eba02e3184105b45","nasal":"22d8e344e26028980834a4d79e039c52d14bd7e356b93b62eba02e3184105b45"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-11-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":11,"verse":21,"english":"Having said this touching Agastya of the splendour of the sun, that son of Raghu took hold of his feet.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.542,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3011021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f0669853c925cee0fa1a867f3a553988343fa5ff79f9a2a1e501d6ec3ffc3d12","compact":"4adb28865f8234d52dc0f350b5d1bf419bb53231910cbe32cf0a5b6e7ec0b020","nasal":"4adb28865f8234d52dc0f350b5d1bf419bb53231910cbe32